What is Aramid Fiber for Ballistic?
Aramid fiber for ballistic is a class of high‑modulus synthetic fibers characterized by an aromatic polyamide backbone. The most widely used variant, para‑aramid, offers an exceptional strength‑to‑weight ratio, enabling designers to replace traditional steel or ceramic plates with lighter, yet equally protective, fabric‑based solutions. Its inherent resistance to heat, chemicals, and fatigue makes it suitable for a broad spectrum of defense and security applications, ranging from personal body armor to armored vehicle panels.
